.TH SUSFILE 1 "2026" "susfile" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
susfile \- CLI file-forensics visualiser
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B susfile
[\fIflags\fR]
[\fIfile\fR]
.br
.B susfile
.B version
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B susfile
reads a single file and shows what it is: magic header, MIME and detected type,
size and timestamps, MD5/SHA\-1/SHA\-256, ELF/PE/Mach\-O structure, Shannon
entropy and ent\-style statistics.
.PP
Its centrepiece is a
.IR "file map" :
the whole file drawn as a grid of block cells where the glyph names the content
class found in that region (source, printable text, machine code, compressed,
encrypted, padding and so on) and the colour encodes the region's entropy.
.PP
With no flags and a terminal on standard output,
.B susfile
launches an interactive TUI. Otherwise it prints a plain text report.
Called with no
.I file
argument in a terminal, it opens the TUI with its filesystem picker ready so a
file can be chosen; with no terminal a missing
.I file
is an error.
.PP
.B susfile
makes no network connections and sends no telemetry.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-no\-tui
Print a plain text report instead of launching the TUI.
.TP
.B \-\-json
Emit a machine\-readable JSON report on standard output.
.TP
.BI \-\-strings\-min " N"
Minimum length for an extracted string. Default 4.
.TP
.BI \-\-max\-bytes " N"
Cap how many bytes are read for the full\-buffer analysis passes. Default
268435456 (256 MiB). Hashing and the global entropy pass always stream.
.TP
.BI \-\-map\-size " WxH"
Grid size for the plain\-mode ASCII class map. Default 64x16.
.TP
.B \-\-allow\-special
Permit analysing non\-regular files such as devices or FIFOs.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-color
Disable colour output. Also honoured via the
.B NO_COLOR
environment variable.
.TP
.BR version ", " \-\-version ", " \-V
Print build metadata and exit.
.TP
.BR help ", " \-\-help ", " \-h
Print usage and exit.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Analysis completed.
.TP
.B 1
The file could not be read.
.TP
.B 2
Usage error.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Inspect a binary in the TUI:
.B susfile /usr/bin/ls
.TP
Scriptable report:
.B susfile \-\-json ./firmware.bin | jq .verdict
.TP
Read from standard input:
.B cat blob | susfile \-
.SH AUTHOR
kawaiipantsu / THUGS. Source at https://github.com/kawaiipantsu/susfile
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR file (1),
.BR xxd (1),
.BR ent (1)
